	"fig-open-oracle-arbitrager-lifecycle": {
		"ariaDescription": "The arbitrager synchronizes approved OpenOracle reports, compares each report with executable Uniswap V2, V3, and hookless V4 liquidity while retaining a Uniswap V3 TWAP anchor, atomically hedges and disputes an eligible report, waits through later dispute rounds, then atomically settles and withdraws exact balances into a provisional finality state that retains risk and evidence. A receipt reorganization returns the position to open, inter-reader disagreement keeps finality pending, and quorum-agreed evidence that conflicts with the durable journal moves the position to recovery. Closure realizes profit only when the configured reader requirement returns twelfth-descendant finality evidence. The primary reader is sufficient by default; quorum 2 requires at least two available readers, and every available response must agree. An immediately replaced reporter follows the separately documented exact-credit path and remains a risk-consuming replaced position.",
		"ariaLabel": "OpenOracle arbitrager execution and recovery lifecycle",
